{"status": "ok", "message-type": "work", "message-version": "1.0.0", "message": {"indexed": {"date-parts": [[2026, 10, 28]], "date-time": "2026-10-28T19:11:51Z", "timestamp": 1793214711121, "version": "4.5.0"}, "reference-count": 51, "publisher": "Society for Industrial & Applied Mathematics (SIAM)", "issue": "6", "content-domain": {"domain": [], "crossmark-restriction": false}, "short-container-title": ["SIAM J. Appl. Math."], "published-print": {"date-parts": [[1990, 12]]}, "abstract": "<jats:p>A simple model for synchronous firing of biological oscillators based on Peskin\u2019s model of the cardiac pacemaker [Mathematical aspects of heart physiology, Courant Institute of Mathematical Sciences, New York University, New York, 1975, pp. 268\u2013278] is studied. The model consists of a population of identical integrate-and-fire oscillators. The coupling between oscillators is pulsatile: when a given oscillator fires, it pulls the others up by a fixed amount, or brings them to the firing threshold, whichever is less.</jats:p>\n                  <jats:p>The main result is that for almost all initial conditions, the population evolves to a state in which all the oscillators are firing synchronously. The relationship between the model and real communities of biological oscillators is discussed; examples include populations of synchronously flashing fireflies, crickets that chirp in unison, electrically synchronous pacemaker cells, and groups of women whose menstrual cycles become mutually synchronized.</jats:p>", "DOI": "10.1137/0150098", "type": "journal-article", "created": {"date-parts": [[2005, 2, 23]], "date-time": "2005-02-23T09:50:11Z", "timestamp": 1109152211000}, "page": "1645-1662", "source": "Crossref", "is-referenced-by-count": 1688, "title": ["Synchronization of Pulse-Coupled Biological Oscillators"], "prefix": "10.1137", "volume": "50", "author": [{"given": "Renato E.", "family": "Mirollo", "sequence": "first", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}, {"given": "Steven H.", "family": "Strogatz", "sequence": "additional", "affiliation": [], "role": [{"vocabulary": "crossref", "role": "author"}]}], "member": "351", "published-online": {"date-parts": [[2006, 7, 10]]}, "reference": [{"key": "R1", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1137/0146015"}, {"key": "R2", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.61.1679"}, {"key": "R3", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.2307/3962532"}, {"key": "R4", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00276000"}, {"key": "R5", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1086/415929"}, {"key": "R6", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1038/scientificamerican0576-74"}, {"key": "R7", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00276069"}, {"key": "R8", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1103/PhysRevLett.61.231"}, {"key": "R9", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1126/science.7433976"}, {"key": "R10", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00276542"}, {"key": "R11", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00276558"}, {"key": "R12", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1137/0515019"}, {"key": "R13", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1137/0150009"}, {"key": "R14", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00276897"}, {"key": "R15", "first-page": "R102", "volume": "246", "author": "Ermentrout G. B.", "year": "1984", "journal-title": "Amer. J. Physiol."}, {"key": "R16", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1137/0146024"}, {"key": "R17", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00275153"}, {"key": "R18", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1515/9780691221793"}, {"key": "R19", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF00276928"}, {"key": "R20", "first-page": "2158", "volume": "37", "author": "Hanson F. E.", "year": "1978", "journal-title": "Fed. Proc."}, {"key": "R21", "doi-asserted-by": "publisher", "DOI": "10.1007/BF0027591